Well... Big party :). After about 6 years I made it. I have to admit I 
ascended in Slash'Em once (search with google groups, same character 
name) before, but S is a complete different game... So I consider this a 
YAFAP :).
I never keep any notes, I don't have the dump patch, so this is a bit 
unclear. But anyway...
Start was nothing big... I'm trying W for a long time now, leaving race, 
gender and alignment random. Gno Fem Neu, it'll be then. No big starting 
inventory, except for a spellbook of magic missile. This became 
extremely valuable. I cleared the way to Sokoban with the help of my 
cat, finished Sokoban (BoH) and went to the mines. Then I realized I was 
gnomish and could have entered before with pretty small risk... But it 
didn't matter. No big things along the way... Until two levels below 
Minetown. A blessed magic lamp. A wish. A blessed fixed +2 silver dragon 
scale mail. Okay... Now with a bit of luck, this can become sweet.
Further things were pretty boring. Not really boring for me, but nothing 
unusual for you out there, I guess. Found an altar about 5 levels above 
the castle... Wrote a spellbook of create monster, sacrifice, sacrifice, 
sacrifice. Got crowned pretty soon, I need to reread the spoilers to get 
more out of that sort of situations. Castle was pretty tense sometimes, 
especially because of the Liches. I genocided them immediately when I 
found a scroll of genocide in the Castle. Wishes went to armor, mostly. 
In fact, I think all of them went to armor.
Quest was easy, Gehennom was boring. Magic mapping proved invaluable, as 
did Identify. Together with a pick-axe, I just made my way from stairs 
to stairs. Had no trouble with the Demon Lords, only Orcus managed to 
beat me hard with some summoned monsters. But I got out of it alive. I 
wore Vlad's AoLS from when I got it till the end, but luckily never 
needed it.
Then I woke the Wizard, no problemo, off to the sanctum, still no 
problemo. Tense moment when entering the sanctum, the high priest was a 
bit tougher then I expected him to be. He got me to 18 hp, that was the 
only time when I used a healing spell... It was really tense, extra 
healing with a failure of 37%. But it worked. And after I healed myself, 
I realised I still had the "oLS :).
The way back up was frustrating with the mysterious force, but once past 
Gehennom, it went really fast. Rush up, to earth. Kill Rodney, kill 
small critters, use confused scroll of gold detection, get /oDigging, go 
to portal. Air, zap levitation, ?oGD, rush towards portal. Charm or 
Finger air elementals on the way. Fire, ?oGD, bit of charm monster, but 
of evasions, rush to the portal. Water, genocide ; (forget about it 
before), charm couple of water elementals, kill others, ?oGD, 
waitwaitwait for portal to appear (I finally discovered it hiding under 
a spellbook, great). Astral, Put on towel, go to Famine, Finger, try to 
get trough the Angels and priests with mostly Magicbane and Finger of 
Death, and the first altar was the right one... I didn't spent 100 turns 
on Astral, I think.

